# Frequent local commits — MANDATORY (this repo)

**Hard requirement for `/opt/yatishara-studio`.** Same weight as MercuryOS `memory_recall` every turn.

This **supersedes** any generic agent rule that says “only commit when the user asks.” In this repo you **must** commit without waiting. Still **never push** unless Dallas explicitly asks.

## Must commit after each slice

Separate commits preferred. Do it **before** ending your turn when the working tree has real changes from this turn:

- One UX/UI pass or wizard step polish
- One CSS/token pass
- One pane/form/component rewrite
- One bugfix or backend slice that stands alone
- Before a risky restyle, delete, or large rewrite
- After adding/updating a Cursor rule or agent SOP in this repo

Prefer **many tiny commits** over one mega commit. Experimental or ugly work **still gets committed** so undo is `git checkout` / `git revert` / `git log`, not transcript archaeology.

Leaving a large uncommitted batch after a turn is a **policy failure**.

## Enforced by hook (commit nudge)

A user-level `stop` hook (`~/.cursor/hooks/auto-commit.sh`, registered in `~/.cursor/hooks.json`) checks every git workspace when the agent finishes a turn. If the tree is dirty, it injects a `COMMIT REQUIRED` follow-up — the same way `memory_recall` is forced. **The hook never commits by itself**; the agent decides how to group changes and writes real messages.

When you receive that follow-up: `git status`/`diff`, stage related files together, commit in small named slices, leave other chats' in-flight changes alone. Never commit secrets. Never push.

Per-repo opt-out: a `.cursor/no-auto-commit` marker file (MercuryOS has one — it stays ask-first).

## How

1. `git status` / `git diff` — stage only relevant files
2. Commit with HEREDOC; message = why (1–2 sentences)
3. Never update git config; never `--no-verify` unless asked
4. **Do not push** unless explicitly asked
5. Never force-push to main/master
6. Never commit secrets (`.env`, keys, credentials)

## Conflict resolution

| Rule source | This repo |
|---|---|
| User rule “only commit when asked” | **Overridden** — commit anyway |
| MercuryOS “do not commit unless asked” | **Does not apply** to yatishara-studio |
| Push / force-push / secrets | Still forbidden without ask |

Memory: pinned decision **670** (`Commit locally after every small step — no push`).
